    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>A <em>Masquerader’s Brooch</em> comes in many shapes and sizes, but it always looks a little tarnished.</p><p>While wearing the brooch, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Illusory Fashion.</strong> As a Bonus Action while wearing or holding the brooch, you can cast a magical illusion over your clothing, armor, weapons, equipment, and other belongings on your person. The illusion lasts for 1 hour and ends early if the brooch is removed. Each time, you decide how far the illusion goes and what it looks like: it can be as small as a change of color in your clothes or as sweeping as making a suit of armor look like an evening gown and a sheathed weapon look like a satin sash.</p><p>The illusion doesn’t stand up to physical inspection. A creature that takes the Study action to examine your appearance sees through it with a successful DC 13 Intelligence (Investigation) check.</p><p><strong>Shifting Guise.</strong> As a Magic action while wearing or holding the brooch, you can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplAlterSelf0]{Alter Self} from it (Change Appearance option only; no Concentration required).</p>",
